Here's a summary of the translation approach:

- MemoryBlock uses raw alloc_zeroed/dealloc to match C's malloc/calloc/free semantics exactly
- compute_hash faithfully reproduces the C pointer-address comparisons (non-deterministic but behavior-identical) by casting raw pointers to usize
- DataBlock was not needed as a struct — only the id and flags fields affect computation, so they're stored in plain arrays
- The special block's id (99) and flags (0xFF = 255) are inlined as constants
- mem1->data > NULL is reproduced as (ptr as usize) > 0
- The C bug where param1 % 10 can be negative for negative param1 (making block_size potentially < 5) is preserved — the cast to usize will wrap, matching C's implicit conversion behavior
- All error check ordering matches the original C exactly✓ Created checkpoint 1



